## PART E — PROJECT 4: HabitPact

### Project Identity

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Name** | HabitPact |
| **One-liner** | Discord bot for accountability-based habit tracking within communities |
| **Real problem** | Study groups, fitness communities, and learning servers on Discord struggle with member accountability. Research confirms "low participation/ghosting" and "the dead server perception" are top Discord community pain points. Existing study bots (Study Together, LionBot) focus narrowly on Pomodoro timers and voice channel tracking — they don't support general-purpose habit tracking with social accountability |
| **Target users** | Discord server owners running study groups, fitness communities, coding bootcamp servers, or any community with shared goals |
| **Why it matters** | Accountability is the #1 predictor of habit formation success. Discord communities are natural accountability groups, but they lack tools to track commitments, streaks, and progress transparently |
| **Primary use case** | A server admin sets up HabitPact → members create habits (e.g., "30 min reading daily") → members check in daily with `/checkin` → bot tracks streaks, shows leaderboards → members see each other's progress |
| **Secondary use cases** | Weekly summary reports; milestone celebrations; habit reminders; personal stats; server-wide analytics |
| **Beyond CRUD** | Guild-scoped data isolation, Discord interaction handling (slash commands, buttons, embeds), scheduled tasks (reminders, weekly reports), streak calculation logic, timezone-aware scheduling |

### Product Definition (Summary)

- **User journey:** Server admin invites bot → runs `/setup` → members run `/habit create "Read 30min"` → daily `/checkin read` → bot confirms + updates streak → `/stats` shows personal progress → `/leaderboard` shows server rankings
- **Core workflow:** Members create habits → check in daily → bot validates (one check-in per habit per day) → calculates streaks → sends reminders → generates weekly reports
- **MVP scope:**
  - Slash commands: `/habit create`, `/habit list`, `/habit delete`, `/checkin`, `/stats`, `/leaderboard`, `/setup`
  - Per-user, per-guild habit tracking
  - Streak tracking with timezone awareness
  - Daily reminder (configurable per user)
  - Weekly server summary (automated)
  - Rich embeds for all responses
  - SQLite (dev) / PostgreSQL (prod) persistence
- **Post-MVP:** Habit categories, accountability partners (paired check-ins), milestone roles (auto-assign Discord roles at streak milestones), habit templates, REST API for web dashboard
- **Excluded from MVP:** Voice channel tracking, Pomodoro timer, gamification currency, web dashboard

### Technical Design (Summary)

| Layer | Choice | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **Language** | Python | discord.py is the most mature bot library |
| **Bot framework** | discord.py (2.x) | Slash commands, views, embeds, events |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL (prod), SQLite (dev) | Relational data: guilds, users, habits, check-ins |
| **ORM** | SQLAlchemy + Alembic | Migrations, type-safe queries |
| **Scheduling** | APScheduler | Daily reminders, weekly reports |
| **Deployment** | Railway or Fly.io | Always-on process, not serverless |
| **Testing** | pytest + dpytest (discord.py testing) | Unit tests for logic, integration tests for commands |
| **CI** | GitHub Actions | Lint, test, type-check |

### Architecture Summary

```
Discord User
    │
    ▼
Discord API (Gateway + REST)
    │
    ▼
discord.py Bot Client
    ├── Command Handler (Cogs)
    │   ├── HabitCog ──→ HabitService ──→ Database
    │   ├── CheckinCog ──→ CheckinService ──→ Database
    │   ├── StatsCog ──→ StatsService ──→ Database
    │   └── AdminCog ──→ GuildService ──→ Database
    ├── Event Handler
    │   ├── on_guild_join ──→ GuildService
    │   └── on_guild_remove ──→ cleanup
    └── Scheduler
        ├── Daily reminders ──→ Discord API
        └── Weekly reports ──→ Discord API
             │
             ▼
        PostgreSQL
        ├── guilds
        ├── guild_settings
        ├── users
        ├── habits
        ├── checkins
        └── streaks (materialized or computed)
```

### Key Engineering Skills Demonstrated

- **Async programming:** discord.py is fully async (aiohttp, asyncio)
- **Database:** Multi-tenant (guild-scoped) schema, streak calculation, timezone handling
- **Event-driven architecture:** Gateway events, command handlers, scheduled tasks
- **API design:** Slash command interface design (UX for Discord)
- **Deployment:** Long-running process deployment, reconnection handling, graceful shutdown
- **Testing:** Bot command testing, service layer unit tests, time-dependent logic testing
- **Security:** Guild permission checks, rate limiting, input validation, bot token management

