## PART G — BUILD ORDER

### Recommended progression: P2 → P4 → P1 → P3

| Order | Project | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **1st** | **EnvGuard** (CLI) | Fastest to a working product. No deployment infrastructure needed. Teaches clean Python architecture, testing, packaging, and PyPI publishing. Builds confidence with a shippable tool before tackling complex systems. |
| **2nd** | **HabitPact** (Discord Bot) | Introduces databases, async programming, and multi-tenant data. Moderate complexity. Teaches event-driven patterns and scheduled tasks. Deployable quickly on Railway. Real users from day one (any Discord server). |
| **3rd** | **StatusPing** (Web App) | Most complex project. Requires frontend + backend + database + auth + background jobs. Benefits from database and API experience gained from HabitPact. Teaches full-stack product engineering end-to-end. |
| **4th** | **ClipVault** (Extension) | Different engineering surface entirely (browser APIs). Benefits from accumulated backend/testing experience. Teaches a unique skill set (content scripts, service workers, browser storage) that complements the other three projects. |

This progression builds skills incrementally: local tool → backend service → full-stack app → browser platform.

